# CODEOWNERS -- who must approve what.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CURRENTLY IN *SOLO MODE* -- everything is owned by @jarvicecore.
#
# `jarvicecore` is a personal account, and personal accounts cannot have teams.
# The enterprise mapping is preserved verbatim at the bottom of this file: move
# this repo into an org, create those six teams, swap the blocks over, and
# re-run `./scripts/bootstrap-github.ps1` (without -Solo).
#
# One thing solo mode CANNOT do: GitHub will not let you approve your own pull
# request. So while you are the only owner, the ruleset must not require
# code-owner review, or every PR deadlocks. That is why
# `./scripts/bootstrap-github.ps1 -Solo` applies rulesets/main-solo.json
# instead of rulesets/main.json.
#
# In solo mode this file is therefore documentation + auto-assigned reviewers,
# not an enforced gate. The moment you have a second human, switch back.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

* @jarvicecore

# --- Pipeline itself -------------------------------------------------------
# Changes to CI/CD are changes to the control plane. Whoever can edit a workflow
# can exfiltrate every secret that workflow can reach.
/.github/workflows/                @jarvicecore
/.github/CODEOWNERS                @jarvicecore
/.github/rulesets/                 @jarvicecore
/.github/dependabot.yml            @jarvicecore
/scripts/                          @jarvicecore

# --- Promotion gates -------------------------------------------------------
# The file that says "prod runs v0.1.42" is the most security-relevant line in
# the repository. Ownership of it is the whole control.
/environments/promotion-path.yaml  @jarvicecore

# dev has no manifest -- it always runs the latest release. Nothing to own.
/environments/qa.yaml              @jarvicecore
/environments/stage.yaml           @jarvicecore
/environments/uat.yaml             @jarvicecore
/environments/prod.yaml            @jarvicecore
/environments/train.yaml           @jarvicecore


# ===========================================================================
# ENTERPRISE MAPPING -- restore this when you move to an org.
#
# Delete everything above, uncomment everything below, create the six teams,
# then run `./scripts/bootstrap-github.ps1` with NO -Solo flag.
#
# The point of this layout is that each environment gets progressively stricter
# ownership. A developer cannot self-merge their way into production, because
# promoting to prod means editing environments/prod.yaml, which requires
# release-managers AND security to sign off.
# ===========================================================================
#
# *                                  @ORG/platform-engineering
#
# /.github/workflows/                @ORG/platform-engineering @ORG/security
# /.github/CODEOWNERS                @ORG/platform-engineering @ORG/security
# /.github/rulesets/                 @ORG/platform-engineering @ORG/security
# /.github/dependabot.yml            @ORG/platform-engineering
# /scripts/                          @ORG/platform-engineering
#
# /environments/promotion-path.yaml  @ORG/platform-engineering @ORG/release-managers
#
# /environments/qa.yaml              @ORG/qa
# /environments/stage.yaml           @ORG/qa @ORG/release-managers
# /environments/uat.yaml             @ORG/release-managers @ORG/business-owners
# /environments/prod.yaml            @ORG/release-managers @ORG/security
# /environments/train.yaml           @ORG/release-managers @ORG/training
